## Responsive Design Rules
- Use a mobile-first approach: start with the smallest screen and layer on complexity
- Breakpoints: `sm:` (640px), `md:` (768px), `lg:` (1024px), `xl:` (1280px), `2xl:` (1536px)
- Stack columns vertically on mobile; use grid/flex layouts on larger screens
- Ensure touch targets are at least 44x44px on mobile
- Hide non-essential elements on small screens rather than cramming content
- Test that no horizontal scrollbar appears at any breakpoint

## Semantic HTML Requirements
- Use proper heading hierarchy: a single `<h1>` per page, then `<h2>`, `<h3>`, etc. in order without skipping levels
- Use landmark elements: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<aside>`, `<footer>`
- Use `<button>` for actions and `<a>` for navigation -- never use `<div>` or `<span>` as clickable elements
- Wrap form inputs with `<label>` elements or use `for`/`id` associations
- Use `<ul>`/`<ol>` for lists of items, not sequences of `<div>` elements

## Performance Best Practices
- Use `loading="lazy"` on all `<img>` elements that are below the fold
- Minimize inline styles; prefer Tailwind utility classes
- Avoid large inline SVGs when a simple icon class or emoji would suffice
- Do not embed base64-encoded images or large data URIs
- Keep the DOM tree shallow where possible (avoid deeply nested wrapper divs)

## Image Placeholder Conventions
- When the original page references images that are unavailable, use placeholder URLs from `https://placehold.co/`
- Format: `https://placehold.co/{width}x{height}/{bg_color}/{text_color}?text={label}`
- Example: `https://placehold.co/600x400/e2e8f0/475569?text=Product+Image`
- Always include descriptive `alt` text on every image element

## Accessibility Requirements
- Every `<img>` must have a meaningful `alt` attribute (empty `alt=""` only for purely decorative images)
- Add `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby` to interactive elements that lack visible text labels
- Ensure color contrast meets WCAG AA: at least 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text
- Include focus-visible styles on all interactive elements (`focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2`)
- Use `role` attributes where semantic HTML alone is insufficient (e.g., `role="banner"`, `role="navigation"`)
- Ensure all form controls have associated labels

